<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/identifier> "012-BFO" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "specifically depends on"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "s-depends on"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(Elucidation) specifically depends on is a relation between a specifically dependent continuant b and specifically dependent continuant or independent continuant that is not a spatial region c such that b and c share no parts in common & b is of a nature such that at all times t it cannot exist unless c exists & b is not a boundary of c"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A shape specifically depends on the shaped object; hue, saturation and brightness of a colour sample specifically depends on each other"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "specifically depends on"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000195> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The analogue of specifically depends on for occurrents is has participant."@en .
