<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(Elucidation) A continuant fiat boundary b is an immaterial entity that is of zero, one or two dimensions & such that there is no time t when b has a spatial region as continuant part & whose location is determined in relation to some material entity"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "As for fiat point, fiat line, fiat surface"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000140> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "continuant fiat boundary"@en .
